    "description": {
      "value": "<p>If there's one people whose curiosity can match a Fenari's, it's the Gnomes. Caravans that settle in Gnomish burrows and workshop-towns find themselves surrounded by kindred spirits: folk who can't leave anything un-poked, un-opened, or un-improved.</p><p>Gnomish Fenari shrink over the generations and develop clever, nimble fingers (and, many swear, larger ears for hearing the tiny clicks of a good mechanism). They take to tinkering with abandon. Every new find gets taken apart to see how it works, and most of the time it even goes back together.</p><p>Their experiments are the stuff of legend in their adopted towns, some for good reasons and some for loud ones. Gnomish Fenari consider a little smoke damage a fair price for discovery, and they tend toward chaotic good.</p><p><strong>Size.</strong> Living among Gnomes has made these Fenari smaller than their kin, most growing between 3'0\" and 3'8\" tall and weighing 35 to 55 pounds. Your size is Small.</p><p><strong>Languages.</strong> Most Gnomish Fenari learn Gnomish.</p><h3>Gnome Culture Traits</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Traits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Tinker, Nosy</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Take It Apart, <em>Identify</em></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Experimental Gadget</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this Culture). You can cast each leveled spell once without a spell slot, regaining the ability when you finish a Long Rest; you can also cast them using any spell slots you have.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
